on: 28039\n\n--- Record 502 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Off-Cycle Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-09\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: 28039\n\n--- Record 503 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.43.1\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Logs: Besides FluentBit, you can now also use OTLP as output for you LogPipeline resources. Based on an OTel Collector, you can tail logs from stdout/stderr, as well as push logs from applications. The gateway enriches your log data in the same way as for traces and metrics. For details, see Application Logs (#556).      Logs, Metrics, and Traces: For all your pipelines using an OTLP output, you can centrally configure enriching the data with Pod labels, so that the data gets k8s.pod.label.label attributes. For details, see Data Enrichment (#2195).      Traces and Metrics: Update to OTel Collector 0.128.0 (#2221).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 504 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing – Corrected Condition Base Calculation for Conditions with Multiple Counters\nDescription: When a condition had multiple counters and the step number was set to zero for that condition, the condition base incorrectly included results from subsequent steps. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 505 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pricing – Validation Fix for Zero-Value Conditions in Price Agreement\nDescription: When a condition was passed with a value of 0.000 and the plus/minus flag was set to negative in the condition type customizing, it incorrectly triggered a validation error in the Price agreement scenario. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-09\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 506 ---\nComponent: Personalized Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Overall Improvements\nDescription: There have been several code, stability, and performance improvements.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 507 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.14\nDescription: New and changed features are available for administration, data cataloging, data integration, data marketplace, data modeling, data privacy and protection, and space management.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.14. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-08\nValid as Of: 2025-07-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 508 ---\nComponent: Responsibility Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Data Centers\nDescription: The Responsibility Management Service is now also available in the following regions:  AWS: EU12 - Europe (Frankfurt)  Google Cloud Platform: US30 - US Central (IA)  Google Cloud Platform: EU30 - Europe (Frankfurt)  See Pricing and Regions Information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-14\nValid as Of: 2025-07-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 509 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Functions for Decisions\nDescription: You can now use a new function, TRUNC in your decisions. See Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-07\nValid as Of: 2025-07-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 510 ---\nComponent: API Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availibility of the Externalization feature on Edge Integration Cell\nDescription: You can now use the externalization feature to define API policies that can retrieve externalized configuration values during runtime. These parameters can be utilized later without modifying the standard API artifact. For more information, see Externalize Parameter for API Artifact.\n\",967\n671,\"--- Record 1291 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Correct Condition Base Calculation\nDescription: The pricing condition used to be inactive (inactiveFlag = \"\"X\"\") when the from-step number in the pricing procedure was greater than or equal to the step number of the condition during the condition base calculation. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1292 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.5\nDescription: New and changed features are available for data integration, data marketplace, data modeling, and others.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.5. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-05\nValid as Of: 2025-03-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1293 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Advanced Functions for Decisions\nDescription: You can now use a new function, DATE in your decisions. See Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-04\nValid as Of: 2025-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1294 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: API Trigger for Decisions\nDescription: You can create an API trigger for a decision to execute this decision using APIs in a shared environment. See Create an API Trigger.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-04\nValid as Of: 2025-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1295 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Export and Import Feature for Documents Used with Instant Learning (Premium Edition)\nDescription: You can now export and import documents that you have edited and confirmed for use with instant learning.  Formerly, instant learning could use your feedback to enhance extraction results only in the client or instance in which you originally edited and confirmed documents. If you changed context, you had to reenter your feedback in the new context.  This new feature on the SAP Document AI basic UI allows you to quickly and easily export documents along with all information relevant for instant learning and import them for use in another context. As a result, you benefit from improved extraction results across different clients and instances, with no additional manual effort.  You can also forward the exported data to your support contact for troubleshooting.  See Export/Import Documents.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-04\nValid as Of: 2025-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1296 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Export Document Details Endpoint\nDescription: The Document API endpoint Export Document Details is now available. Use it to export information that is associated with a document, such as ground truth and related instant learning data.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-04\nValid as Of: 2025-03-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1297 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Additional selected models and model versions from Open AI are supported.  For more information, see 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1298 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Responses in markdown format from orchestration and prompt editor apps will be rendered in the response window, where supported by the chosen model.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1299 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Best Practices for Outlook Activities\nDescription: You can now send emails on behalf of someone in Outlook.See Send Emails on Behalf of Someone in Outlook.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-03\nValid as Of: 2025-03-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1300 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Excel SDK\nDescription: Various Microsoft Excel activities are added to enhance the Microsoft Excel SDK.You can now use the Get Sensitivity Label ID activity to retrieve the sensitivity label ID of the current workbook, the Set Sensitivity activity to set a sensitivity to the current workbook, the Get UsedRange Row (from file) to retrieve the row index of the used range in the ac